1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ilancueitl (Nahuatl for "old-woman skirt"; pronounced [ilaŋˈkʷeː.itɬ]) is a significant female founding figure in the histories of the ruling dynasty of Tenochtitlan, though her precise role is described differentl
2 CONC y in different sources. She is associated with Acamapichtli, the first ruler of Tenochtitlan; according to one source (the History of the Mexicans as Told by Their Paintings), she was the first ruler of Tenochtitlan herself.
2 CONT
