1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Quaquapitzahuac (died 1407) was the first tlatoani (ruler) of the Aztec city of Tlatelolco. He was a son of Tezozomoc, the Tepanec ruler of Azcapotzalco. His name, which means "Slender Horn", was pronounced [kʷaːkʷ
2 CONC aʍpiˈtsaːwak] in Classical Nahuatl, and is also spelled Cuacuauhpitzahuac , Cuacuapitzahuac, and Quaquauhpitzahuac.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his death in 1407 he was succeeded by his son Tlacateotl.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT His name is also spelled Cuacuauhpitzahuac , Cuacuapitzahuac, and Quaquauhpitzahuac.
