2 CONT Atotoztli (Classical Nahuatl: Atotoztli /atoˈtostɬi/) or Huitzilxochtzin (Classical Nahuatl: Huitzilxōchtzin /witsiɬˈʃoːtʃtsin/) was a daughter of the Aztec emperor Moctezuma I and Chichimecacihuatzin, the daughter of Cuauhtototzi
2 CONC n, the ruler of Cuauhnahuac.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Tezozomoc, son of the previous emperor Itzcoatl, and gave birth to three sons who would later become emperors themselves: Axayacatl, Tizoc, and Ahuitzotl.
