1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Schmal, John P.; ''Moctezuma's Descendants in Aguascalientes''  ...  ''Tracking the offspring of the last Aztec monarch''  ...  [LatinoLA: January 8, 2014]  ...  http://latinola.com/story.php?story=12449
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the author Donald E. Chipman (''Moctezuma's Children: Aztec Royalty Under Spanish Rule'', 1520-1700, pp. 70-71),  …  “Two years later in '''1531''', Mariana married her second husband, '''Cristobal de Valderrama'''. D
2 CONC on Cristobal, '''a native of Burgos, España''', was a '''conquistador who served in Michoacán, Colima and Zacatula'''. The History of Tarímbaro (Michoacán) states that Cristobal de Valderrama was '''given the encomienda of Tarímba
2 CONC ro (1526-1537) and of Ecatepec''', and he is mentioned in the text of Michoacán's early history during the 1530s until '''his death in November 1537'''. Mariana and Don Cristobal had only one daughter, Leonor de Valderrama y Mocte
2 CONC zuma, who was baptized sometime around 1532. Chipman discusses this family on pages 76 through 77 of his book.”
