1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Don Juan Cano de Saavedra (c. 1502–1572) was a Spanish conquistador from Cáceres in Extremadura.
2 CONT
2 CONT At age 18, Cano travelled to the New World and took part in Pánfilo de Narváez's expedition against Hernán Cortés. Cano subsequently fought for Cortés after Narváez's defeat.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1532 Cano married Isabel de Moctezuma (Tecuichpotzin), principal heir of Moctezuma II, becoming her third Spanish husband. The couple had five children: Pedro, Gonzalo, Juan, Isabel, and Catalina. Both daughters became nuns.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cano died in Seville in September 1572.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Juan Cano Saavedra nació en la villa de Cáceres, Extremadura. En 1519 Cano se encontraba en Cuba, de donde pasó a la Nueva España con Pánfilo Narváez, tomando parte en la conquista de Tenochtitlán. 
