1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Don Cristóbal de Guzmán Cecetzin (or Cecepaticatzin) was a colonial Nahua noble from Santa María Cuepopan in San Juan Tenochtitlan. A son of the ruler don Diego Huanitzin, don Cristóbal first served as alcalde in 1
2 CONC 556 before becoming Tenochtitlan's second-last tlatoani and third governor in 1557, titles he held until his death in 1562.
