1 NOTE In the last will and testament of Hernan Cortes he gives a fortune to his daughter born of a Cuban Taino Indian who was born in old Cuba. In his testament he states that he had Catelina baptised and given the family name of his mo
2 CONC ther, Catalina Pizarro. This must have enflamed his legitimate wife, Juana, and must have been a big blow to her ego -  him having had so many "wives" besides her.
2 CONT There is a big possibility that Catelina Pizarro might have been a Ciboney Taino woman. In any case, when the future finally arrived all of his descendants of Indigenous blood did very well as far as working the games that surroun
2 CONC ded the mayorazgos that bound distinguished families together. If you have the patience, please do take the time to travel within the many branches of the family tree of Hernan Cortez de Pizzaro, Emperor Moctezuma and his descenda
2 CONC nts right down into the Nieto de Silva.
2 CONT
