1 OCCU Teniente de Captain General of the Viceroy, Don Martin Enriquez de Almanza, Soldier
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A member of a prominent Granada family, he had come to the Indies in 1516.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jose Antonio Esquibel reported in SHHAR (Vol. I, 1994) titled "Lines of Descent from Don Alfonso XI, Rey de Castilla y Leon, to Don Ruy Diaz de Mendoza y Arellano" in which he presented eight lines of descent linking King Alfonso 
2 CONC XI to Ruy Diaz de Mendoza y Arellano.  Esquibel states that this Ruy Diaz de Mendoza y Arellano was "...presumably the same man of this name who was the husband of doña Catalina de Salazar...".
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ES.28079.AHN/1.1.1.12.4.1//OM-EXPEDIENTILLOS,N.1083    
2 CONT
2 CONT Zaldívar, Vicente de
2 CONT
2 CONT Fecha Formación:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1628
2 CONT
2 CONT Acording to his son Vicente's genealogy, in the document above, he was born in Vitoria
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for LT. CAPTAIN GENERALVICENTEDE SALDIVAR-Y-ONATE:
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the lieutenant captain general of the Viceroy, Don Martin Enriquez de Almanza.
2 CONT
2 CONT This viceroy's served the king of Spain from November 5, 1568 to October 3, 1580.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''': From the books ''Don Juan de Onate Colonizer of New Mexico'' by George P. Hammond and ''Northern New Spain, A research Guide'' by Thomas C. Barnes, Thomas H, Nayor, and Charles W. Polzer
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT General Vicente de ZALDIVAR400,918 was born about 1529. Parents: Ruy Diaz de ZALDIVAR and Maria Perez de OÑATE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Magdalena de MENDOZA y Salazar. Children were: Vicente de ZALDIVAR, Juan de ZALDIVAR, Cristobal de ZALDIVAR, Ana de ZALDIVAR (aka Magdalena de Mendoza).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b248.html#P995
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Vicente de ZALDIVAR498,3025 was born (date unknown). Vicente took the surname of his maternal grandfather. Parents: Diego GARCIA de Quintanilla and Mariana de ZALDIVAR (aka Mariana or Maria Ana de Sosa).
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Maria de TREVIÑO. Maria de TREVIÑO and Vicente de ZALDIVAR were married after 6 September 1686.3025
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b248.html#P3595
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================
2 CONT
2 CONT  Vicente de Zaldívar, the elder, and Magdalena de Mendoza y Salazar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Zaldívar and Oñate families of Zacatecas were charter members of a "silver aristocracy" that had discovered and developed mines at Zacatecas in the late 1540s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *ZALDÍVAR, JUAN DE (ca. 1570–1598). Juan de Zaldívar, Spanish soldier and explorer, was born on the mining frontier of northern Mexico about 1570. His parents were...
2 CONT *ZALDÍVAR, VICENTE DE (ca. 1573–?). Vicente de Zaldívar, the younger, Spanish explorer and soldier, was probably born in Zacatecas, a mining town on the frontier of northern Mexico, about 1573. He and Juan de Zaldívar were sons of
2 CONC  Vicente de Zaldívar, the elder, and Magdalena de Mendoza y Salazar. ....before 1620 he married Juan de Oñate's daughter, María de Oñate.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/online/articles/fza06
