1 NOTE The name "Ruy Dias de Mendoça" appears in the account books of Isabel la Catolica, dated mainly from 1483-1504, so this may be a reference to this Ruy Diaz or perhaps his father
1 NOTE The name "Ruy Dias de Mendoça" appears in the account books of Isabel la Catolica, dated mainly from 1483-1504, so this may be a reference to this Ruy Diaz or perhaps his father
1 NOTE Birth Notes: The birthdates available for Vicente de Zaldivar Y Oñate range from c. 1512 at the earliest to c. 1540 at the latest so it is possible that one generation in this line has been missed by researchers. Since Vicente ser
2 CONC ved with Guzman in 1530 (see notes) the 1512 date would seem to be accurate but this perhaps makes him rather old to have his children (bet. 1560 and 1575) as has been recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: Many references are made to one Vicente de Zaldivar in connection with the Oñate Expedition but these references are to Vicente de Zaldivar Y Oñate's son, born c. 1563. It is presumed that Vicente did not go with hi
2 CONC s son on the expedition with Oñate and that he may have in fact died previously.
2 CONT
2 CONT See note for Vicente's de Zaldivar (son) for more information on his participation in this expedition.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • He immigrated.
2 CONT
2 CONT • He immigrated in 1534 to Nueva Galicia. 496 Listed as a conquistador that served with Nuno de Guzman on his expeditions into Nueva Galicia (Aguascalientes, San Luis Potosi, Jalisco and Zacatecas) in 1530.
2 CONT
2 CONT Zaldivar, Vicente de
2 CONT of: Quetaria, Gp.
2 CONT to Mexico:1534
2 CONT parents: Ruy Diaz de Zaldivar and Marina Perez de Onate wife: Magdalena de Mendoza.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see entry for brother, Juan.
2 CONT
2 CONT • He was employed in New Spain. 497 Silver mine owner in Zacetecas, New Spain. See entry for son, Vicente de Zaldivar, for more information on the families silver mining.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • He immigrated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see entry for brother, Juan.
