1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hernando de Hinojos and his brother Sebastián appear in the 1597 Casco roll of Oñate's forces as natives of Cartaya, Condado de Niebla, the sons of Juan Ruiz. He was thrity-six years old in 1598, and is described a
2 CONC s having a good stature and a chestnut beard. Again he is mentioned as a native of Cartaya (Cartaya, Condado de Niebla, Andalusia, España ), the son of Juan Ruiz and the brother of Sebastián.
2 CONT
2 CONT When members of the colony deserted, Hernando was among the Loyalists who stayed in New México. His brother wasn't as lucky, he was killed at Acoma pueblo in 1598.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is mentioned again as a captain, and then as a Procurator General for the Kingdom of New México when he accompanied the wagon-trains in 1613 and 1617. He was married to Beatriz Pérez de Bustillos, was was mentioned to be his wi
2 CONC dow by 1632.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two known sons of theirs were Miguel and Juan, and they had a daughter named Gerónima. Gerónima married Francisco de Anaya.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Origins of New Mexico's Families, pg. 48
2 CONT
2 CONT The Origins of New México Families, pgs. 48, 51, 76, 38, 42, 86
2 CONT
2 CONT Hernando married Beatriz Pérez de Bustillo, daughter of Juan Pérez de Bustillo and María de la Cruz. (Beatriz Pérez de Bustillo was born in 1593 in Ciudád de México, Nueva España 274 and died after 1631.)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://cybergata.com/roots/5572.htm
