2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT And in-law to Don Juan Perez de Oñate. Don Juan Guerra was a Silver baron from Zacatecas. Financial backer of the 1598 Oñate entrada unto New Mexico. In 1599, during the second expedition into New Mexico, he was named lieutenant g
2 CONC overnor and captain general by Don Juan Perez de Oñate. Source: From the book's; Land of the Conquistadores by Cleve Hallenbeck.
2 CONT
2 CONT A History of New Mexico by Gaspar Perez de Villagra, Alcala - 1610, translated by Gilberto Espinosa. The Last Conquistador, Juan de Onate and the settling of the far Southwest, by Marc Simmons. Historia del Nuevo Reino de Leon, by
2 CONC  Eugenio del Hoyo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Juan de Oñate Colonizer of New Mexico, by George P. Hammond.
2 CONT
2 CONT New Mexico's First Colonists, compiled and arranged by David H. Snow.
2 CONT
