1 NOTE Born in the Basque Country and moved to the city of Victoria in Alava where he was called Juan de Onate. In the Basque Language, Onate means at the foot of the Mountain Pass. One of his sons Cristobal de Onate came to New Spain pr
2 CONC obably in 1524. Cristobal participated in the conquest of Jalisco Zacatecas, and Culican. He married Catalina de Salazar in New Spain, She was a daughter of the Royal Treasurer officer for New Spain, Gonzalo de Salazar and Catalin
2 CONC a de la Cadena . Cristobal's father in law, was a son of El Doctor Fernandez de Guadalupe, a famous Royal Physiscian who was a Converso. Catalina de la Cadena was a descendant of the wealthy Converso house of Maluenda. Cristobal a
2 CONC nd Catalina's son, Juan de Onate the conquerer of New Mexico, was born in Zacatecas adn in turn Married a Daghter of Hernan Cortes, and a Granddaughter of Emperor Moctezuma. Juans Gen eology shows how a descendant of Basques and C
2 CONC onveros through his marriage form ed a new bond between the old and new world, Many of Juan de Onate's Descendant s are settled through Mexico nad USA.
