2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Served as a page to Ferdinand and Isabella. His parents were members of the court of the Catholic Kings. His father was known ad "El doctor de Guadalupe."
2 CONT
2 CONT The Encomenderos of New Spain, 1521-1555
2 CONT
2 CONT  By Robert Himmerich y Valencia
2 CONT
2 CONT Gonzalo de Salazar was the royal factor, or business manager for the treasury in New Spain. He came to New Spain in 1524 on the same ship as Cristobal de Onate. Marc Simmons writes "In all respects, Salazar proved to be an unsavor
2 CONC y character, described by contemporaries as a master of subtle duplicity.". Salazar secretly attacked Hernan Cortes' loyalty to Spain and made plans to take over the government of New Spain. When Cortes departed on an expedition t
2 CONC o Central America in late 1524, Salazar and a fellow officer, Pedro Almindez Cherino, quickly took over the government. In Cortes' absence, Salazar also appropriated for his own use the huge estates of Cortes. Cortes was gone on h
2 CONC is expedition until May 1526 and was unaware of what had happened. But, upon his return, Salazar and Cherino quickly lost the power and authority. Regardless of that fact, Gonzalo retired very comfortably and was known as "El Gord
2 CONC o".
