1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fernán_Álvarez_de_Toledo_y_Loaysa Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernán Álvarez de Toledo y Loaysa married in 1385, probably in the city of Toledo, to Elvira de Ayala, Lady of Cebello belonging to the powerful House of Ayala and daughter of Diego López de Ayala and his wife, Teresa de Guzmán.1 
2 CONC They had as children:
2 CONT
2 CONT García Álvarez de Toledo y Ayala (m. 1444), III lord of Oropesa, 2 Jarandilla de la Vera and Tornavacas. He married about 1411 with '''Juana de Herrera''', being the junction of the future counts of Oropesa.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://dbe.rah.es/biografias/40824/garcia-alvarez-de-toledo
2 CONT
2 CONT García Álvarez de Toledo
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Álvarez de Toledo, García. Señor de Oropesa (III). ?, ú. t. s. xiv - Oropesa (Toledo), 1444. Noble.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Fernán Álvarez de Toledo, second lord of Oropesa, and Elvira de Ayala, lady of Cebolla and the castle of Villalba in Toledo.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father in 1398 as a minor, so he remained under the tutelage and curatorship of his mother until the year 1403, when he personally took over the government of his lordships. García had grown up as a maid in the ch
2 CONC amber of King Henry III.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Monarch, apparently, had him in such consideration that, when he died in 1406, he allocated a legacy of 15,000 Maravedi in his will. His services to the Crown, first to Henry III, then to the regent Ferdinand and, finally, to 
2 CONC John II, brought him juicy benefits. The third lord of Oropesa always maintained an unshakable loyalty to John II, from the year 1420, when the coup d'état of Infante Enrique de Aragón took place in Tordesillas, until his death in
2 CONC  1444. He always supported the Monarch in all the confrontations that took place between Juan II and his private Álvaro de Luna, on the one hand, and the Infants of Aragon, on the other. Already in 1408 he had obtained a juro of 1
2 CONC 5,000 maravedíes per year in the alcabalas of the wine and the butcher shop of Plasencia.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was the prize he received for his loyalty to the regent and for the promise of sending a host to the Granada campaign that Fernando undertook a year later.
2 CONT
2 CONT A new prebend received in 1422, after the failure of the coup of Henry of Aragon, when John II granted him nothing less than the privilege of carrying the royal rapier in the solemn ceremonies of the Court.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1428 the Monarch also donated to him, not without the opposition of the city city concil, the martiniegas of Salamanca.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the traditional strategy of the lineage, he contracted a good marriage with Juana Núñez de Herrera, a daughter of another powerful lord of the Extremadura region, Marshal García González de Herrera.
2 CONT
2 CONT García Álvarez de Toledo y Ayala III Señor de Oropesa, Señor de Jarandilla de la Vera y Tornavacas
2 CONT 1386–1444
2 CONT BIRTH ABT. 1386 • Oropesa, Toledo, España
2 CONT DEATH 1444 • Oropesa, Toledo, España
2 CONT
