2 CONT
2 CONT Royal Crown Restored, pg. 47
2 CONT *Census: Don Diego de Vargas, 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693, El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thirty-ninth household, one daughter, one stepdaughter, and two of her children
2 CONT
2 CONT Doña Bernardina Trijillo, widow of Captain Andrés Hurtado, with one daughter named doña Mariana Salas Orozco, eighteen; and one stepdaughter named Juana, with two daughters and one son, named Maria, fourteen: Bernardina, eight; an
2 CONC d José, four.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal Crown Restored, pg. 47
2 CONT *Dates & Events. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernardina was a member of the Diego de Vargas party that returned to New Mexico in 1693, after the Pueblo Revolt of 1680 drove the Spanish New Mexican settlers out of New Mexico. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hurtado children were numerous. Lucía de Salazar (Salas or Hurtado), was the wife of Captain Don Fernando Durán y Cháves. Isabel de Salazar was the third wife of Juan Lucero de Godoy. María de Salazar was married to Manuel Bac
2 CONC a. Mariana married Manuel Vallejo and her sister Catalina was the wife of José Gallegos. Daughter, Juana, was captured by the Pueblo people during the revolt, was later rescued by her brother Martín in 1692. There were at least fo
2 CONC ur brothers, Andrés, Diego, Francisco and Martín.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT The Origins of New México Families, pg. 49
2 CONT * Livestock Distribution, 1697, Santa Fé, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España. 
2 CONT
2 CONT doña Bernardina de Salas, widow with dependents, Bernarda and Berardina, 4.5 varas of wool, 3.75 of baize and 9 mantas
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Blood on the Boulders II, pg. 1151
2 CONT *Dates & Events, 1706. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernardina de Salas y Trujillo was among the founding mothers of Alburquerque in 1706.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernardina married Andrés Hurtado Captain, son of Pedro Hurtado and Catalina de Salazar, By 1652 in Bernalillo, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España.[252] (Andrés Hurtado Captain was born in 1628 in Zacatecas, Nueva Galicia, Nueva España [2
2 CONC 52] and died in 1679 in Santa Fé, Santa Fé, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España.)
2 CONT --------------------
