2 CONT
2 CONT "The peninsular trunk of the López de Elizalde, according to the information cited, was the marriage formed by Miguel López de Lizarde or López de Lizalde (or de Lizarde, or de Lizalde) and his wife María de Aberruza, neighbors wh
2 CONC o were the Town of Tolosa in the Province of Huipuscua (Guipúzcoa). Of them it is known that they were "original Biscayans, who were and had in the said Town of Tolosa by People clean of known houses and Lots, and as such they alw
2 CONC ays enjoyed the exceptions and freedoms enjoyed by the Hijosdalgo." Miguel López de Elizalde and his wife María de Aberruza lived in Tolosa in the mid-16th century; and were the parents of: a) Juan López de Elizalde y de Aberruza"
2 CONC [1 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Juan López de Elizalde y Aberruza, originally from Tolosa, Navarra Guipúzcoa, was the son of Miguel López de Elizalde and Leonor de Aberruza; Leonor Becerra y Sánchez de Mendoza was the daughter of Juan Becerra and Ana Sánchez de
2 CONC  Mendoza, the latter daughter of Toribio Hernández de Arrellano and Isabel Hurtado de Mendoza, both with their ancestry documented." [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding [3]
2 CONT On January 21, 1585, Juan López and Leonor Becerra were married and watched, witnessed by Lorenço Alvares, Juan Ruis, and Diego Martin...
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Ruiz
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
