1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wedding [1]
2 CONT On the 27th day of December [1636] he married Luis de los Reyes according to the order of Holy Mother Church with Juana de Vargas; witnesses Martín Pérez, Hernando de Alva, Juan de Vargas, having preceded the provisions of the Hol
2 CONC y Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dⁿ Gerónimo de Pinedo y Carvajal
2 CONT Year of 1637, Don Gerónimo de Pinedo y Carvajal being Vicar
2 CONT Velose - On seven days of the month of February of that year I gave the nuptial blessings to Luis de los Reyes and Juana de Vargas according to the order of Our Holy Mother Church. His godparents were Juan de Vargas (Machuca) and 
2 CONC Catalina de Ayala.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dⁿ Gerónimo de Pinedo y Carvajal
2 CONT
2 CONT Testament [2]
2 CONT In the name of Almighty God amen. Please know how many of you see this letter from my will, like me Luís de los Reyes , resident of this town of Aguascalientes, legitimate son of Luís de Murguía and María de la Cruz, neighbors who
2 CONC  were from Mexico City, now deceased, being sick with a disease that our Lord was pleased to give me, in my entirety, just as our Lord has given it to me, considering that every living being is mortal...etc. etc
2 CONT
2 CONT And ten, I declare that I am married and veiled following the order of our holy mother church with Juana de Tiscareño and through our marriage we have had and procreated by our children Juan de los Reyes María de la Cruz, Luisa de
2 CONC  los Reyes, Isabel de Tiscareño, and Luís de los Reyes, Josepha, Inés, Juana, Theresa and Antonio de los Reyes, all our legitimate children, of whom Juan de los Reyes, María de la Cruz, Luisa de los Reyes and Isabel are married to
2 CONC day. of Tiscareño, declare it for the record.
2 CONT
2 CONT And ten, I declare that at the time and when I became married to the said my wife Juana de Tiscareño, her aunt María de la another amount of pesos that I do not remember in detail, but it will be stated in the letter of dowry in y
2 CONC our favor that I have granted, which in passing before Joseph Leaño, notary of His Majesty, to which it is sent to me, which it seems to me that it contains a dowry It will be one thousand four hundred and fifty pesos and at that 
2 CONC time my wealth would be a little more than one hundred pesos and one mule with which I began to work.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yten. I declare as my assets the houses of my residence with its annex and belongings, four rooms and barns, all covered with andiron and raja, all new......etc."
2 CONT
2 CONT Death [3]
2 CONT Luis de los Reyes, Spanish, husband of Juana de Tiscareño, confessed and received the holy sacraments, and his executors were Juana de Tiscareño, his wife and Juan de los Reyes, his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT On January twenty-fourth, year one thousand six hundred and seventy-five, I buried Luis de los Reyes , her neighbor, Juana de Tiscareño's husband, in the parish church of this town, who confessed and received the holy sacraments. 
2 CONC He left a novena of restored masses offered as is customary and left twenty masses prayed for the souls in purgatory and for their deceased servants. Likewise, I order thirty masses prayed for his soul to be said. He leaves no wor
2 CONC k behind and his executors were Juana de Tiscareño, his wife, and Juan de los Reyes, his son, and for the record I signed it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolome de Soto y Carvajal
2 CONT Fuentes
