2 CONT <p><p style="text-align: left;" dir="ltr">&nbsp;</p></p><p><h1 id="firstHeading" class="firstHeading" style="text-align: justify;" lang="en">Gaspar Alfonso P&eacute;rez de Guzm&aacute;n, 9th Duke of Medina Sidonia</h1></p><p><div 
2 CONC id="bodyContent" class="mw-body-content"></p><p><div id="siteSub" style="text-align: justify;">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div></p><p><div id="contentSub" style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</div></p><p><div id="jump-to
2 CONC -nav" class="mw-jump" style="text-align: justify;">Jump to: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaspar_Alfonso_P%C3%A9rez_de_Guzm%C3%A1n,_9th_Duke_of_Medina_Sidonia#mw-head">navigation</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wik
2 CONC i/Gaspar_Alfonso_P%C3%A9rez_de_Guzm%C3%A1n,_9th_Duke_of_Medina_Sidonia#p-search">search</a></div></p><p><div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-content-ltr" style="text-align: justify;" lang="en" dir="ltr"></p><p><p><strong>Gaspar Alf
2 CONC onso P&eacute;rez de Guzm&aacute;n y Sandoval, 9th Duke of Medina Sidonia</strong> (1602&ndash;1664) became <a title="Duke of Medina Sidonia" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_of_Medina_Sidonia">Duke of Medina Sidonia</a> i
2 CONC n 1636, upon the death of <a title="Juan Manuel P&eacute;rez de Guzm&aacute;n, 8th Duke of Medina Sidonia" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Manuel_P%C3%A9rez_de_Guzm%C3%A1n,_8th_Duke_of_Medina_Sidonia">Juan Manuel P&eacute
2 CONC ;rez de Guzm&aacute;n, 8th Duke of Medina Sidonia</a>.</p></p><p><p>In 1622, aged 20, he married his 15-year-old aunt <a class="new" title="Ana Mar&iacute;a de Guzm&aacute;n (page does not exist)" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/
2 CONC index.php?title=Ana_Mar%C3%ADa_de_Guzm%C3%A1n&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1">Ana Mar&iacute;a de Guzm&aacute;n</a> (1607&ndash;1637), having four children by her, of which only the youngest,Gaspar Juan, survived to inherit the tit
2 CONC le.</p></p><p><p>In 1639 the 9th Duke was married for a second time to Seville noblewoman Juana Fern&aacute;ndez de C&oacute;rdoba, but only after signing documents giving the considerable amount of 20,000 <a title="Ducat" href="h
2 CONC ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ducat">Ducados</a> to <a class="new" title="Margarita Mara&ntilde;on (page does not exist)" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Margarita_Mara%C3%B1on&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1">Margar
2 CONC ita Mara&ntilde;on</a>, on condition she become a nun near his palace in <a title="Sanl&uacute;car de Barrameda" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanl%C3%BAcar_de_Barrameda">Sanl&uacute;car de Barrameda</a>, later in a Dominica
2 CONC n convent. It is said she was the mother of his illegitimate daughter, Luisa.</p></p><p><p>In 1640, his sister <a class="mw-redirect" title="Luisa of Guzman" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luisa_of_Guzman">Luisa of Guzman</a>
2 CONC  became the new Queen of Portugal, as the wife of the former Duke of Braganza, now <a title="John IV of Portugal" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_IV_of_Portugal">John IV of Portugal</a>. In 1641 the 9th Duke led the <a ti
2 CONC tle="Andalusian independentist conspiracy (1641)" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andalusian_independentist_conspiracy_(1641)">Andalusian rebellion against Spanish rule</a>. Though both Portugal and Catalonia had strong cultur
2 CONC al identities, an historical record of independence, and popular support, Andalusia did not, and the rebellion failed. The duke had the support of his brother-in-law, <a title="John IV of Portugal" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w
2 CONC iki/John_IV_of_Portugal">John IV of Portugal</a>, but the promised naval aid from France and the Netherlands did not arrive. The king of Spain forgave his treason, but the previous prestige of his house was only regained by his su
2 CONC ccessor.</p></p><p><table class="wikitable succession-box" style="margin-bottom: 0.5em; font-size: 95%; clear: both; margin-top: 0.5em;"></p><p><tbody></p><p><tr><th style="border-top: #ace777 5px solid;" colspan="3"><a title="Spa
