1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Maria Hurtado de Salas''' born about 1657, died on 22 Mar 1726 in Santa Fé, Santa Fé, Nuevo México, Nueva España and was buried in 1726 in Conquistadora Chapel, Santa Fé, Santa Fé, Nuevo México, Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Antonio de Montoya, about 1639 in Nuevo México, Nueva España. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria was the daughter of Capitan Andrés Hurtado and Bernardina de Salas y Trujillo, 
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''To The Royal Crown Restored'', pg. 37:
2 CONT
2 CONT She appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT >First household, three sons, five daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT >First, I (Vargas) visited the household of captain Antonio Montoya, alcalde ordinario de segundo voto, married to María Hurtado, with eight children, three boys and five girls; Juan, eighteen, Andrés, fourteen, and Antonio, nursi
2 CONC ng; Juana, thirteen; María, eleven; Antonia, seven; Nicolasa, five; Tomasa, three.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT   Adopted along with 2 others by Bernardina de Salas Trujillo and Andres Hurtado from the Zuni Pueblo, said to be her husbands daughters from an indian wife..
2 CONT --------------------
