1 OCCU Captain, Spanish Soldier, 1692+Census+-+Cristobal+Baca+II, +wife+Ana+Moreno+de+Lara, +&+kids. (Cristobal Baca II, wife Ana Moreno de Lara, & kids are named on the 1692 Census.) 1692 El Paso del Norte, Nuevo México, New Spain
1 TITL Capitán
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Cristóbal Baca''' born c. 1635, Bernallilo, Nuevo Méjico, Nuevo España, died 11 Apr 1697, Bernallilo, Nuevo Méjico, Nuevo España. He died at about the age 62.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was part of troops assembled on October 2, 1680, at La Salineta, New Mexico. Cristóbal Baca was referred to as a nephew of Antonio Baca. He signed the muster-roll Recording his rank as captain, that he was married, with three g
2 CONC rown sons and three daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son-in-law of Diego de Trujillo. Both individuals were persecuted by the ill-famed Governor, López Mendizábal.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Cristóbal married Ana Moreno de Lara Trujillo, daughter of Diego de Trujillo and Catalina Marquez Vásquez, about 1639 in Santa Fé, Santa Fé, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España. (Ana Moreno de Lara Trujillo was born about 1639 in Santa Fé,
2 CONC  Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España and died after 1693 in Santa Cruz de la Cañada, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España.)
