1 OCCU He also took the oath to serve his majesty in the provinces of New Mexico, Married in 1560 in Mexico City- Beyond Origins of NM Families
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There are a few different theories on who this Juan de Vaca was and where he originated, but there are no primary sources to confirm these speculations.   There were four recorded Juan de Vaca's that came to the Ne
2 CONC w World from 1520-1539.
2 CONT
2 CONT Recently, researchers discovered documents that may shed light on Cristóbal Baca’s ancestry. It must be noted that these are just promising leads, and should not be taken as absolute proof. As mentioned before, Juan de Vaca was th
2 CONC e father of Cristóbal Baca. Baptismal records were discovered for three children of a certain Juan Baca and Juana de Zamora. These baptisms took place in the 1560s and 1570s, around the same time that Cristóbal was purported to ha
2 CONC ve been born. Since one of Cristóbal’s daughters was named Juana de Zamora, it is argued that she may have been named after her paternal grandmother and thus this couple are Cristóbal’s parents. It was not unusual for a Spanish ch
2 CONC ild at that time to given the surname, if not the full name, of a grandparent.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is further argued that a certain Cristóbal Vaca and Mayor Díaz may have been the parents of Juan de Vaca. A baptismal record from 1540 shows this couple as the parents of Baltazar Vaca. This couple could have easily been one ge
2 CONC neration younger than Juan, and therefore could have also been his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another Juan de Vaca, from Mayorga, is recorded as settling in Mexico in 1538. His parents were Nuño de Vaca and Beatriz de Quiñones. He was a conquistador with the Coronado Expedition 1540-1542.  
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT There were 4 recorded Juan de Vaca's that came to the New World from 1520-1539. Of these, one from Mayorga is recorded as settling in Mexico in 1538. His parents were Nuno de Vaca and Beatriz de Quinones. Possibly the father of Cr
2 CONC istobal de Vaca.
2 CONT --------------------
