1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the English Wikipedia page on the Baca Family of New Mexico:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baca_family_of_New_Mexico
2 CONT
2 CONT The progenitors of the Baca family of New Mexico were Cristóbal Baca (Vaca) and his wife Ana Ortiz. Cristóbal was a military captain who arrived in 1600 with his family in order to help reinforce the colony. At the time, he had th
2 CONC ree grown daughters and a small son. The Bacas had another son while living in New Mexico.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Cristóbal, the son of Juan de Vaca, was born in Mexico City c. 1567. His wife, also from that city, was the daughter of Francisco Pacheco. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ortiz/Pacheco line
2 CONT
2 CONT Some researchers have discovered an erroneous link between Crístobal Baca’s wife Ana Ortíz and Cristopher Columbus, among others. As noted previously, Ana Ortíz was the daughter of one Francisco Pacheco. At least three separate ar
2 CONC ticles published in genealogical journals have identified this man as Francisco Pacheco de Cordóva.[8] Not only have researchers found that Pacheco de Córdova had an impressive lineage, but so did his wife Juana de la Cueva y Tole
2 CONC do Colón.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana Ortíz has also been shown to related to the famed explorer Francisco Vásquez de Coronado and Francisco Enriques, the Duke of Alburquerque.[9] The problem with this finding is that Francisco Pacheco de Córdova, and assumedly hi
2 CONC s wife, would have been too young to have been the parents of Ana Ortíz. Pacheco was born in 1573. Ana Ortíz’s daughter Isabel de Bohórquez was born c. 1586. Therefore, Pacheco would have been only 13 years older than the woman wh
2 CONC o would supposedly have been his granddaughter.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes:
2 CONT
2 CONT *8. ^ Beerman, “The Ancestors of Alvar Nuñez Cabeza be Vaca”; Jaskolski, Ernie, “The Francisco Vasquez Coronado Connection to New Mexico Descendants” in The New Mexico Genealogist, September 1995: Vol. XXXIV, No. 3; and, Sanchez, 
2 CONC Ernest J., “Beyond Origins of New Mexico Families: The Cristóbal Colón (Christopher Columbus), Francisco Vásquez Coronado, and Francisco Enriques (Duque de Alburquerque) Connection to Doña Ana María Ortiz” in Herencia, January 199
2 CONC 9: Vol. 7, issue 1
2 CONT *9. ^ Sanchez, “Beyond Origins: Crístobal Colón, et al.”
