1 OCCU Member 1598 Onate August 18, 1598 (Age 15 years)   Defending Pueblo January 1599 (Age 16 years) San Juan de los Caballeros, New Mexico, USA, Defending Pueblo January 1599 (Age 16 years) San Juan de los Caballeros
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She came to New Mexico with the Oñate Party of 1598.
2 CONT
2 CONT The village of Bernalillo was named after Pascuala Bernal.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a story about her that took place north of Bernalillo in the Pueblo of San Juan. In January of 1599, there was word that a hostile Native Americans approaching the Pueblo. Pascuala and about 24 armed women went to the roo
2 CONC f tops to defend the Pueblo.
2 CONT
2 CONT When it was asked, who is ready to defend San Juan, a fellow female comrade, Eufemia, stood and said they were ready to defend the Pueblo. Oñate showed pride for the women, and they all stood up & fired into the air.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pascuala married Juan de Griego who traveled from Greece to New Spain. They came to New Mexico in 1598 with their children who were all identified as mestizo. Pascuala was a native from the Valley of Mexico, and one of her adult s
2 CONC ons, also named Juan Griego spoke the Aztec's language, Náhuatl. He also served as an interpreter of the Tewa language as well as receiving an encomienda in New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Parientes, La Herencia, Spring 2006
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT # DEATH: BEF 1626 [3292]
2 CONT
2 CONT # EVENT: member 98 Oñate: 18 AUG 1598 [3293] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [3292] [S2200] ORIGINS OF NM FAMILIES
2 CONT
