1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''José Téllez Girón''' aka José Télles Jirón born 1631 died 1695, age 64
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Catalina-Tellez-Giron/6000000008019915347?through=6000000008019959205 Catalina Romero]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of José Téllez Girón and Catalina Romero:
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Jos%C3%A9-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000001500789489?through=6000000008019915347 José Téllez Girón]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Jacinta-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000001500789465?through=6000000001500789489 Jacinta Téllez Girón]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Juan-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000013126728851?through=6000000001500789465 Juan Téllez Girón]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Rafael-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000001500789433?through=6000000013126728851 Rafael Téllez Girón]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Isabel-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000008019864362?through=6000000001500789433 Isabel Téllez Girón]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Catalina-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000013126695736?through=6000000008019864362 Catalina Téllez Girón]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Lucia-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000013126572129?through=6000000013126695736 Lucia Téllez Girón]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Zapata/6000000013126624193?through=6000000013126572129 Maria Zapata]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Juana-T%C3%A9llez/6000000013126723030?through=6000000013126624193 Juana Téllez ]
2 CONT
2 CONT José Téllez Girón is the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Bartolome-Jiron/6000000001500789700?through=6000000008019959205 Bartolome Téllez Girón]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT He appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth household, five daughters, five dependents
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain '''José Téllez Girón''', married to doña Catalina Romero, with one daughter named Jacinta Téllez Girón and another named Maria Zapata.  He states that he has a daughter, a young woman named Juana José Téllez, with his brot
2 CONC her, Juan Téllez Girón.  She writes to his son to bring her.  He also states that he has two other children, Lucia and Catalina, and five dependents, named Gertrudis, Maria, Josefa, and Isabel, and Nicolas.  As a loyal vassal of h
2 CONC is majesty, he is quite ready to enter whenever I, the governor and captain general, enter to settle this kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had the encomiedas of the Pueblo San Felipe and Pueblo Cochiti in 1661. He was married and had four children . He lived in Senecu in 1667, when he claimed to be 35 or 36 years old and a native of Alto de San Jacinto in Cuyocan.
2 CONC  He escaped with the refugees to El Paso del Norte, taking his wife, three sons and four daughters. The next year in 1681 he stated being 49. His daughter Isabel married Jacinto Sanchez de Inigo. He died 1695- Ysleta Del Paso, (Te
2 CONC xas) Kingdom of New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT About two weeks after the Pueblo Revolt in 1680, Jose was at Soccoro with the colonists who survived the massacre in the southwest part of the Kingdom. As Captain with the military , he participated in the decision to take the sur
2 CONC vivors south to meet wagon trains due any time from Mexico. They wanted to go to the rescue of the Governor and other colonist who escaped from Santa Fe but they were out of ammunition and there were too few men with horses.
2 CONT
2 CONT The rest of the family survived including his wife, four sons and three daughters. In 1681they were living in the new community created by the refugees of Spanish colonists and Indians from isetla Pueblo. They called the settlemen
2 CONC t Yselta del Paso in what is now Texas near El Paso.They had no food due to a drought.
2 CONT
2 CONT When time came to return to New Mexico in 1693, he said he was ready to resettle with his family. However Jose and Catalina remained in Yselta del Paso, where he died in 1695. Some of the family did return to New Mexico and one of
2 CONC  them was the daughter Isabel that had married Jacinto Sanchez de Inigo and their two small children. Jacinto and his family returned to Santa Fe in 1693 and in 1703 Jacinto was granted the land near the Pueblo of Cochiti that had
2 CONC  belonged to his father in law Captain Jose Tellez Giron,prior to the Pueblo Revolt in 1680
