2 CONT
2 CONT Died without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalina is the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Captain-Jos%C3%A9-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000008019959205?through=6000000008019915347 Captain José Téllez Girón] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Catalina-Romero/6000000008
2 CONC 019915347 Catalina Romero]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT She appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth household, five daughters, five dependents
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain José Téllez Girón, married to doña Catalina Romero, with one daughter named Jacinta Téllez Girón and another named Maria Zapata.  He states that he has a daughter, a young woman named Juana José Téllez, with his brother, J
2 CONC uan Téllez Girón.  She writes to his son to bring her.  He also states that he has two other children, Lucia and '''Catalina''', and five dependents, named Gertrudis, Maria, Josefa, and Isabel, and Nicolas.  As a loyal vassal of h
2 CONC is majesty, he is quite ready to enter whenever I, the governor and captain general, enter to settle this kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3
