1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cristóbal Enríquez, was beheaded in 1643 for his role in the assassination of New Mexico Governor Rosas.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a first cousin of Agustín de Carvajal. (Pg. 15 "Origins"). Their mothers were sisters.  In 1660 Agustin was accused of marrying his close relative, Estefania Enriquez, Cristóbal's daughter. Estefania was a second cousin of 
2 CONC Agustin's first wife, María Márquez.
