1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Antonio Jorge (Abt 1570-) María Álvarez del Castillo (Abt 1574-)
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Jorge Álvarez
2 CONT * Born: 1592, Tangier, Portuguese North Africa 250,322  
2 CONT * Marriage: Ana de Vera Delgado in 1630  
2 CONT * Died: Sep 1655, Nueva España at age 63 
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel married Ana de Vera Delgado, daughter of Gaspar de Vera and María Delgado, in 1630. (Ana de Vera Delgado was born about 1609 in Nueva España.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: Manuel's will is online as part of the Beyond Orgins collection, 7 Jun 1655. 250 
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel signed his will on his death bed. He lists 9 legitimate children.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Gilbert T. Maldonado has published on article on the same topic, "Origins of Manuel Jorge from His Last Will and Testament," in Herencia Vol. 10, Issue 1, January 2002: 31-44, and presents a translation of the primary source docu
2 CONC mentation, the last will and testament of Manuel Jorge Álvarez, recorded at San José de Parral in 1655. Maldonado presentation of the information is conclusively confirms that Antonio Jorge de Vera was a son of Manuel Jorge Álvare
2 CONC z and Ana de Vera Delgado and that Manuel Jorge, the armorer was a brother of Antonio." ~ ~  Source: Archivo Historico de Parral, Roll 1654B, fr. 942 - 945, fol. 72r - 74v; San José de Parral, Parral Hidalgo, México, Matrimonios, 
2 CONC 1632-1660, LDS #0162555
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service, 1648, Parral, Nueva España
2 CONT
2 CONT In records, Manuel Jorge is referred to as the armorer or blacksmith who was imprisoned by Governor Mendizábal in 1661. In 1658, he received pay as an official Armorer of New México, and was appointed in 1655. ~The Origins of New 
2 CONC México's Families, pg. 51
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  Manuel Jorge Álvarez
2 CONT * Born: 1592, Tangier, Portuguese North Africa 250,322  
2 CONT * Marriage: Ana de Vera Delgado in 1630  
2 CONT * Died: Sep 1655, Nueva España at age 63  
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel married Ana de Vera Delgado, daughter of Gaspar de Vera and María Delgado, in 1630. (Ana de Vera Delgado was born about 1609 in Nueva España.)
2 CONT
