1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There is a lot about him in the Spanish archives on line, though the texts are very difficult to read. Martin was constantly fighting or engaging in litigation with his eldest brother, the family heir. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Someone took out my data and put theirs in. Please do not do this again. This was originally my profile. From numerous historical documents in the Spanish archives on line that I've read, Martin acknowledged that the heiir of the 
2 CONC Casa de Zaldivar was Pedro, his elder brother. He repeatedly refers to Pedro as the Head of the House of Zaldivar, or as "el primogenito" or first son. Using Saenz instead of Ruiz also indicates that he is not the eldest son. He m
2 CONC ay have chosen Saenz because the original founders' names were Rodrigo (Ruiz) Sanchez: the first son here takes the name Ruiz, reserved for the eldest and the heir. The second son takes the name Sanchez or Sanches to indicate that
2 CONC  he is not the heir. However this is a strategic move since the Zaldivars counted King Sancho II of Navarra as their ancestor.
