1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://books.google.com/books?id=4cUo8JqYztoC&pg=PA129&lpg=PA129&dq=Santiago+del+Riego,+Royal+Audiencia+of+New+Spain&source=bl&ots=dBkBubIGE6&sig=36a9kcC5J81a3HtlA6CGhbaPzWQ&hl=en&sa=X&ei=8tjsVOHAM4m-ggS7vYOgDg&v
2 CONC ed=0CCYQ6AEwAg#v=onepage&q=Santiago%20del%20Riego%2C%20Royal%20Audiencia%20of%20New%20Spain&f=false Martínez, María Elena.  ''Limpieza de Sangre, Religion, and Gender in Colonial Mexico'', Stanford University Press, Stanford, Cali
2 CONC fornia, 2008, page 129]   ...  "'''Del Riego was the illegitimate son of a nun whose ancestry could for obvious reasons not be investigated without damaging her honor and that of her convent.'''" [Footnote #24 cited.]
2 CONT
