1 NOTE Alcalde Mayor Salinas District, "Attlia"-[
2 CONT
2 CONT "Nicolás de Aguilar was a native of Yurirapundaro, Michoacán. He was the son of Pedro de Aguilar, deceased, and of Isabel de Villagómez, a native of the same village. His maternal grandparents were Fernando de Villagómez, an origi
2 CONC nal Conquistador of Michoacán Province, and Luisa Pérez, also born in the same village. When eighteen years old, Nicolás left his widowed mother and went to the northern frontier settlement of Parral, where he worked as a miner an
2 CONC d soldier for six years. From here he fled to New Mexico after committing a murder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aguilar lived in New Mexico for some time prior to 1660, serving as an unscrupulous lackey of Governor López Mendizábal. As Alcalde Mayor of the Salinas district he persecuted the missionaries with devilish fury and humor. The fri
2 CONC ars referred to him as "Attila". Finally he was summoned before the Inquisition on Mexico City, where he had to answer for his crimes; found guilty, he was banished from New Mexico for ten years and deprived forever of holding any
2 CONC  office.
2 CONT
2 CONT On coming to New Mexico he had married Catalina Márquez, daughter of Francisco Márquez and Maria Nuñez of Santa Fe. At the time of his trial, between 1660 and 1665, they had four children: Geronima, Maria, Isabel and Nicolas. An Y
2 CONC nez de Gracia, living in the Salinas country near Cuarac, was mentioned as being his sister-in-law. After this, no more is heard of Aguilar. The family either followed him to New Spain, or stayed in New Mexico under their mother's
2 CONC  name, and with good reason." 339
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Migration: 1645, Parral, Nueva Vizcaya, Mexico. Worked here as a miner and soldier for six years. Fled to New Mexico after committing a murder.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Migration: 1651, , , New Mexico. Fled to New Mexico after committing a murder.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Special: 1645, Parral, Nueva Vizcaya, Mexico. Committed murder according to Chavez.
2 CONT
2 CONT was a miner
2 CONT
2 CONT fled to New Mexico, around 1660 when he murdered someone.
