1 NOTE This is what I'd like to add to the Ortiz de Parada and Ulloa tree.
2 CONT 	1. It looks so bare on the top, left and after all, it's got Ortiz de Paradas.  Please add a son of Capt. Joseph and Elvira, with his wife:
2 CONT 	Capt. Diego Ortiz de Parada and his spouse, Nicolasa González de Laris, owners of "Las Mesillas" in Lagos.  Her parents were Fulgencio González de Ruvalcaba y Rodas and María de Laris y Tavera.
2 CONT 	2. Extreme top part, right: The complete surname of Catalina López is Catalina López de Lamadrid.  Repeated further down, as she's the mother of Juana Muñoz de Jerez.  (She'll appear again, you"ll see.)
2 CONT 	3. The genealogy of Elvira Aguilar Ventosillo.
2 CONT 	Parents: Captain Alonso de Aguilar Ventosillo and María de Busto.  Oh, and missing is Elvira's carta de dote (dowry) in León, on 9 March 1660.
2 CONT 	Nothing else on the Aguilar Ventosillos.
2 CONT 	Maternal Grandparents: Alonso de Busto, born in León and a miner in Guanajuato.  Declared his will 30 April 1645 in León, before Melchor de Ledesma, Escribano Público.  Marriage "velación" in Lagos on 20 July 1616 to Ana de J
2 CONC erez.
2 CONT 	Next, Alonso de Busto's parents were Pedro de Busto and Leonor Díaz de Noriega, natives of Boca de Huérgamo, León, Spain.  They came to New Spain and settled in León.
2 CONT 	The parents of Ana de Jerez were Rodrigo Muñoz de Jerez and Catalina López de Lamadrid.  (You see?)
2 CONT 	So, Capt. Joseph Ortiz de Parada and Elvira Aguilar Ventosillo were blood relatives in the third degree (second cousins).  And both were, with Capt. Pedro de Ulloa y Márquez in the same degree.
2 CONT 4. A bottom note that related to these persons by both the Busto and Muñoz de Jerez lineages, was Francisco Matías de Busto y Moya, Muñoz de Jerez y Monroy, a "caballero" of the Order of Calatrava and the first Marqués de San 
2 CONC Clemente.
2 CONT
2 CONT I've got four children identified on Jacinto and Juana, of which just a daughter, María de Laris (no Sáenz or Sáez), married to Fulgencio González de Ruvalcaba y Rodas
