1 CONT Catalina Vásquez was the wife of Diego de Trujillo, and most likely a daughter of Bernardina, from whom her grand-daughter, Bernardina de Salas y Trujillo, got her name
0 @N6000000005024494046@ NOTE Catholic
1 CONT ASENCIO de ARECHULETA was one of the Oñate Soldiers who came in 1598. He was 26 years old, the son of Juan de Arechuleta and a native of Eibar in Guipuzcoa. He is described as having a medium build, black beard and a slight wound 
1 CONC on the forehead. At the famous battle of Acoma, 23 January 1599, he accidentally shot his bosom partner-in-arms Lorenzo Salado de Ribadeneira. In 1603 he escorted four friars from Mexico City to San Gabriel. During Governor Peralt
1 CONC a's term, 1610-1614, he acted as an ecclesiastiacal notary and was thus involved many a fracas which resulted in a strong anti-Peralta faction composed of Archuleta's relatives, "of whom there were many." Asencio was dead by 1626,
1 CONC  when he was cited as living three or four years previously, and when he was the sindic of the Franciscans. 
1 CONT His wife was Ana Perez de Bustillo, daughter of Juan Perez de Bustillo, and they had a son, Juan. One daugher, María was the wife of Captain Juan Marquez; another, Lucia, married Diego de la Serna; a third, unnamed, was the wife o
1 CONC f Matias Lopez del Castillo; a fourth, Gregoria, married Diego de Santa Cruz.
1 CONT __________________
1 CONT Son of Juanes de Arechuleta, native of Ybar, of medium stature, black bearded, a small scar on his forehead, 26 years of age.
1 CONT ASENCIO de ARECHULETA was one of the Onate Soldiers who came in 1598. He was 26 years old, the son of Juan de Arechuleta and a native of Eibar in Guipuzcoa. He is described as having a medium build, black beard and a slight wound 
1 CONC on the forehead. At the famous battle of Acoma, 23 January 1599, he accidentally shot his bosom partner-in-arms Lorenzo Salado de Ribadeneira. In 1603 he escorted four friars from México City to San Gabriel. During Governor Peralt
1 CONC a's term, 1610-1614, he acted as an ecclesiastiacal notary and was thus involved many a fracas which resulted in a strong anti-Peralta faction composed of Archuleta's relatives, "of whom there were many." Asencio was dead by 1626,
1 CONC  when he was cited as living three or four years previously, and when he was the sindic of the Franciscans. 
1 CONT His wife was Ana Pérez de Bustillo, daughter of Juan Pérez de Bustillo, and they had a son, Juan. One daugher, María was the wife of Captain Juan MÁRQUEZ; another, Lucia, married Diego de la Serna; a third, unnamed, was the wife o
1 CONC f Matías López del Castillo; a fourth, Gregoria, married Diego de Santa Cruz.
1 CONT __________________
1 CONT Son of Juanes de Arechuleta, native of Ybar, of medium stature, black bearded, a small scar on his forehead, 26 years of age.
