1 CONT Bartolome de Salazar had been Alcalde Mayor of the Zuñi  and Moqui jurisdiction when he died prior to 1662. His widow was a certain Marta. This woman seems to have belonged to the Martin Serrano and Martin Barba groups of Las Sali
1 CONC nas and so could be the Marta Martin, widow of Bartolome de Ledesma, thus making Salazar and Ledesma the same man. But this is by no means a certainty. 
1 CONT
1 CONT A daughter, from descriptioins given, was a Juana de Salazar, born at Zuñi , who was the wife of Diego Lujan and the mother of Sebastian Lujan. A son, perhaps, was an Agustin de Salasar, who is met at the time of the Reconquest.
